  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 286.13pt, "No equivalent clean-up methods are available in the three software programs. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 306.77pt, "Therefore, the maximum allowable clean-up routines compliant with ISO 13067 (≤ 5 % ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 327.53pt, "change to EBSD map) were performed in AZtecCrystal (remove wild spikes, remove ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 348.17pt, "zero solutions level 2) and OIM Analysis (neighbour orientation correlation level 2). ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 368.93pt, "AZtecCrystal’s ‘Autoclean’ function, which for this dataset is compliant with ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 389.57pt, "ASTM E2627 (≤ 10 % change) but not ISO 13067, was also tested. The MTEX method ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 410.33pt, "[13] is different: by default, it does not clean-up the EBSD map, but assigns the map ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 430.97pt, "area to grains by interpolating unindexed regions. The effective ‘change’ to the EBSD ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 451.73pt, "map is therefore equal to the fraction of unindexed points (6.69 % for this data). The ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 472.39pt, "code to implement this is ")
