  #line-at(85.104pt, 207.74pt, "the majority of the map area is excluded as edge grains (green grains). The area-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 228.38pt, "weighted grain size is underestimated for small image fields, because large grains are ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 249.14pt, "statistically more likely to intersect the map edges and be excluded.  ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 277.85pt, "The Miles-Lantejoul correction, recommended in ISO 13067, recognises that the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 298.49pt, "probability that a grain cuts a map edge is equal to its length fraction perpendicular to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 319.25pt, "that edge, and the grain size distribution may be weighted to correct the bias towards ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 339.89pt, "excluding larger grains [14]. However, this is not trivial to implement practically in AM ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 360.65pt, "microstructures, where a wide range of grain shapes and aspect ratios can contribute to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 381.29pt, "each histogram bin: for example, a long and thin grain is more likely to cut the map ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 402.05pt, "edge than an equiaxed grain with similar grain area.  ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 430.73pt, "A better area-weighting method is shown in the cumulative histograms in Figure 3b. ")
