  #line-at(85.104pt, 152.3pt, "Three AM parts were made by selective laser melting using the same powder and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 172.94pt, "identical build parameters except for the laser power variation mode (square, sinusoidal, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 193.7pt, "triangular waveform). EBSD maps were acquired from four different SEMs using a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 214.34pt, "wide range of experimental parameters, and spatially binned to match the step sizes to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 235.1pt, "as close as possible to 2.5 μm. All maps had at least 90 % indexing and 11 grains along ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 255.74pt, "the build direction. A 10° boundary threshold angle was used throughout.  ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 284.45pt, "The uncertainty component from grain clean-up was calculated from the difference ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 305.21pt, "between no clean-up and maximum possible clean-up, and treated as a Type B ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 325.85pt, "uncertainty with rectangular distribution. The uncertainty component from grain size ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 346.61pt, "histogram binning was the histogram bin half-width, and treated as a Type B uncertainty ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 367.25pt, "with rectangular distribution. The uncertainty component from microstructure sampling ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 388.01pt, "was calculated from 30 bootstrap subsamples as described in Section 2.5 while ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 408.65pt, "maintaining the same map length along the build direction, and treated as a Type A ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 429.41pt, "uncertainty. These were converted to standard uncertainties, combined by adding in ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 450.05pt, "quadrature, and finally expressed as an expanded uncertainty with coverage factor k = 2.   ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 478.75pt, "Table 2 shows the average grain sizes of these three parts, expressed as median indexed-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 499.51pt, "area-weighted MFDs, and as well as another Ni-base superalloy from an unrelated AM ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 520.15pt, "build for comparison. Figure 6 shows grain size maps and cumulative histograms of the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 540.91pt, "grain size distributions of the same maps. The average grain size and grain size ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 561.55pt, "distributions of the three similar AM parts are similar, whereas unrelated Ni sample has ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 582.31pt, "a very different grain size and size distribution. Maps which are shorter along the build ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 602.95pt, "axis have more stochasticity and tend to overestimate the grain size at higher quantile ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 623.71pt, "values, which is consistent with the bootstrap analysis results in Figure 4. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 652.39pt, "Any potential effect of laser power variation mode (triangle, sinusoidal or square) on ")
